1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,829
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,980 --> 00:00:07,630
In this lesson, we will represent
apparatus, crews, and gps devices.

3
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:11,700
A vehicle name alone does not tell a
dispatcher its type, home

4
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,700
station, crew, or location source.

5
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:18,599
We will explain the features, the setup
decisions, and a

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,689
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:24,610
Engine 1 and Rescue 1 are added with their
unit types

8
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:26,360
and assigned to Station 1.

9
00:00:26,529 --> 00:00:30,080
Units let dispatchers send the right
resources and let everyone

10
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:32,119
see which apparatus is available.

11
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:36,219
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:36,219 --> 00:00:38,670
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:43,420
Units. Your apparatus, vehicles and
response teams.

14
00:00:43,639 --> 00:00:46,610
Add each unit with its type and home
station group.

15
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:51,849
Unit types. Categories such as Engine,
Ladder or Ambulance.

16
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:56,599
Create unit types before adding units so
each unit can be classified.

17
00:00:57,410 --> 00:01:02,689
Hardware location tracking. GPS devices
that report unit locations.

18
00:01:02,899 --> 00:01:06,180
Register each tracking device and link it
to its unit.

19
00:01:06,939 --> 00:01:10,360
New Unit. Add an apparatus, vehicle or
team.

20
00:01:10,559 --> 00:01:14,799
List your apparatus or response teams with
their types and home stations.

21
00:01:15,029 --> 00:01:19,700
Teams that respond only as individuals can
mark this module not applicable.

22
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:23,639
Unit Staffing. Assign crew members to
units.

23
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:28,090
List your apparatus or response teams with
their types and home stations.

24
00:01:28,330 --> 00:01:32,979
Teams that respond only as individuals can
mark this module not applicable.

25
00:01:33,779 --> 00:01:38,699
For the training scenario, work in this
order. Step 1. Create Engine

26
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:44,429
and Rescue unit types. Step 2. Add Engine
1 with its type, Station 1,

27
00:01:44,589 --> 00:01:49,949
and crew roles. Step 3. Assign the crew
and, when used, register

28
00:01:49,949 --> 00:01:52,059
a tracking device against the unit.

29
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:54,459
Now verify the result.

30
00:01:54,709 --> 00:01:59,029
Confirm the unit type, home station, crew,
and status.

31
00:01:59,259 --> 00:02:02,839
For hardware tracking, check a recent
received position and

32
00:02:02,839 --> 00:02:04,589
the stale-position behavior.

33
00:02:04,769 --> 00:02:10,009
A common problem to watch for: An old GPS
position is not a live position.

34
00:02:10,179 --> 00:02:15,190
Crew assignment, reported unit status, and
physical readiness are distinct.

35
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,839
Your practice task is simple.

36
00:02:18,009 --> 00:02:21,759
Create Engine 1 in the demo department and
verify the assigned

37
00:02:21,759 --> 00:02:23,379
crew from the dispatcher view.

38
00:02:23,559 --> 00:02:25,759
Measure incomplete unit records.

39
00:02:25,949 --> 00:02:30,469
Record the result, who owns the follow-up,
and when it should be reviewed.

40
00:02:30,599 --> 00:02:34,559
Use the linked feature scripts for the
detailed screen recording plan.

